# Cursor Cloud specific instructions

These notes apply only to Cursor Cloud agents. They cover the toolchain this environment actually provides.

## Toolchain

Vite+ (`vp` 1.4.0) manages Node and pnpm. This repo pins Node 26.12.1 (`package.json` `engines.node`) and pnpm 12.14.0 (`packageManager`). Login shells source `~/.config/vite-plus/env`, which puts `~/.local/share/vite-plus/bin` ahead of `/exec-daemon`. `/exec-daemon/node` is an older Node and is not the version this repo runs. Shells that do not source that env file still see it first, so use `bash -lc` or prepend the Vite+ bin directory.

`native/resource-monitor` is Rust edition 2024 and needs rustc >= 1.85. This image uses rustup's stable toolchain (`/usr/local/cargo/bin`). Linux desktop native modules also need `build-essential`, `pkg-config`, `libsecret-1-dev`, and ImageMagick.

Playwright's Chromium headless shell for web and server tests lives under `~/.cache/ms-playwright`.

## Running the web app

From the repo root, `vp run dev` starts the contracts watcher, the Vite web app, and the server. Read the real ports from the `[dev-runner]` line. On a main checkout, state is `~/.t3`. A linked worktree uses that worktree's `.t3` and ignores an ambient `T3CODE_HOME`.

Leave `VITE_HTTP_URL` and `VITE_WS_URL` unset. Vite proxies `/api` and `/ws` through the page origin. Do not point a server at another machine's `~/.t3/userdata`.

Startup prints `pairingUrl:`. Open that full URL once. The bare origin does not authenticate a new browser.

`vp run dev` registers the free `Replay (dev)` provider. Its Showcase model plays a recorded turn through the real UI. Codex and the other provider CLIs are not installed here, so a Codex health warning in the UI is expected.

## Mobile

This environment has no Android SDK and no emulator. Native mobile builds are out of scope. `vp run lint:mobile` and package typechecks still run.
